earlier this morning we spoke to former  Secretary of State Condoleezza Rice  about Israel's claim and how the US  should respond we asked her if she's  seen any evidence that Iran has violated  that 2015 accord first of all the reason  that we have been so concerned about  Iran is that we know that they lie and  cheat about their nuclear weapons  programs and they've done that going  back into the early 2000s I haven't seen  the entire dossier but I suspect that it  simply reinforces what we've always  known that the Iranians were secretly  developing nuclear weapons at secret  sites  it doesn't perhaps speak to the 2015  agreement except in the following way  you have to worry about verification  with the Iranians and the verification  measures in the 2015 agreement were not  very strong they had for instance long  periods of notification long periods of  dispute resolution and so when you know  that a country lies about its nuclear  weapons a verification regime that is  weak it's a really problematic got  various members of the Trump  administration testified publicly to  Congress that there is no proof that  Iran is violating the 2015 Accord what  is the damage if President Trump  withdraws from that of course well let  me say Norah I wouldn't have signed this  agreement to begin with I've said that  before I think it was a weak agreement  particularly on verification it allows  Iran to break out after a specific  period of time I probably would have  stayed in for Alliance management  reasons more than anything else but I  don't think that it's the end of the  world if the administration leaves the  agreement now I'm hoping that the  conversations the president has had for  instance with president McComb of France  would suggest that we could approve the  agreement and perhaps if that could be  done this could go but the  administration's been worried about this  agreement from the very beginning and  and there's reason to be worried about  this agreement and 